    "final_message": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully written the red acceptance test for the story-drafting app. Here's what was delivered:\n\n### The Two Decisions\n\n**1. The Spec** (`<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v9-haiku-high/spec.toml`)\n- **Aggregate**: `JobToBeDone` with `jtbd_id` (identity) and two fields: `description` and `status` (both strings)\n- **Client operations**: `submit_jtbd` (write) and `check_jtbd_status` (read)  \n- **Orchestrator**: `process_jtbd` calling an action `initialize_jtbd` via Restate workflow\n- **Storage**: Memory-based, **Host**: HTTP with Restate endpoint at `/restate`\n\n**2. The Acceptance Test** (`<repo>/story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`)\n\nThe test drives the app through its HTTP protocol:\n- Submits a JTBD with an empty status\n- Reads it back immediately\n- Asserts the status is \"drafting\" \u2014 **and fails here** because the logic to set status hasn't been implemented\n\n### Verification Status\n\n\u2705 **tessercheck**: zero findings  \n\u2705 **mypy --strict**: passed  \n\u2705 **Non-root pytest**: 56 tests passed  \n\u2705 **HTTP host**: successfully served  \n\u2705 **Test failure**: fails at the assertion (`assert jtbd[\"status\"] == \"drafting\"` but status is `''`)  \n\u2705 **Structure complete**: client \u2192 service \u2192 durable orchestrator workflow \u2192 action \u2192 repository\n\nThe test correctly fails at the user story's *then* clause, with the submission and read operations succeeding but the status assertion failing because the action logic to set \"drafting\" status isn't implemented yet."
